{
  "table_id": "Table_S17",
  "display_number": "S17",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S17. Candidate machine-learning models and LightGBM predictive scenario analysis",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. Seven machine-learning algorithms were evaluated within a common training-test split (N_train = 4,734; N_test = 1,180). All candidate models achieved negligible held-out explained variance (R²_test range −0.006 to 0.005). LightGBM was retained as the final model for the SHAP and scenario analyses but also achieved negligible held-out explained variance (R²_test = 0.0045; RMSE_test = 14.99; best_iteration = 9). Scenario contrasts from this model are therefore descriptive outputs and should not be interpreted as causal intervention effects. A participant-level re-evaluation (60/20/20 participant-level split) confirmed the absence of out-of-sample skill (test R² = -0.013; Supplementary Note on predictive analyses and Supplementary Table S30). Abbreviations: GAM, generalised additive model; GBM, gradient boosting machine; LightGBM, light gradient boosting machine; MAE, mean absolute error; MAPE, mean absolute percentage error; PLS, partial least squares; RAE, relative absolute error; RMSE, root mean squared error; RRSE, root relative squared error; SHAP, Shapley additive explanations."
  ],
